WEBVTT

00:00:02.715 --> 00:00:05.356
The relay is a small MCP server that you host.

00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:09.031
With it, Claude AI can reach the specs on your Mac from claude.

00:00:09.031 --> 00:00:12.189
ai, the Claude app, or Claude Code on another computer.

00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:20.607
Ask Claude AI to send a spec a message.

00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:23.985
It finds the spec through the relay, and sends the message.

00:00:30.486 --> 00:00:33.402
The message reaches the spec's Claude session on the Mac.

00:00:33.402 --> 00:00:37.545
Claude makes the change and answers, and the answer goes back through the relay.

00:00:46.183 --> 00:00:47.287
Later, ask again.

00:00:47.287 --> 00:00:52.870
Claude reads the spec through the relay: its stage, its pull request, and the answer.

00:01:06.709 --> 00:01:11.689
Claude AI connects to the relay over HTTPS, and signs in with your owner password.

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:16.972
The Spec Studio agent on your Mac connects out to the relay, so the Mac opens no port.

00:01:21.198 --> 00:01:26.282
The relay keeps a copy of each spec, the messages, and the sign-ins in a store.

00:01:26.282 --> 00:01:31.430
So Claude AI can read your specs, and leave messages, while the Mac is offline.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.712
The store is pluggable, and you choose one of two.

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.139
The default store is JSON files on a volume.

00:01:43.139 --> 00:01:46.952
The relay is one container and a volume, with no other service.

00:01:46.952 --> 00:01:49.991
With no store settings, the relay uses JSON files.

00:01:55.007 --> 00:02:02.235
If you already run Temporal, the relay can keep the same data in your namespace instead, on Temporal Cloud or self-hosted.

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:05.078
Set the Temporal address and your payload keys.

00:02:05.078 --> 00:02:07.685
The relay encrypts every payload with them.

00:02:11.911 --> 00:02:13.572
Attachments are optional.

00:02:13.572 --> 00:02:20.746
Set the four bucket settings for R2, S3, MinIO, or any S3-compatible service, and messages can carry files.

00:02:20.746 --> 00:02:23.204
Attachments never go into the store.

00:02:23.204 --> 00:02:27.654
With no bucket, the relay works the same, but with no attachments.

00:02:33.645 --> 00:02:37.245
Run the relay with Docker Compose, the Helm chart, or Docker.

00:02:37.245 --> 00:02:41.493
Each release publishes a signed image for Intel and Arm, and the chart.

00:02:44.512 --> 00:02:49.110
The relay guide takes you through each step, from the password to the connector in Claude AI.
